  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607184500: Bounded HTTP body completeness and browser/Node high-level parity

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-18

## Decision

The Kotoba HTTP provider performs repeated transport reads into a caller-sized
bounded buffer until EOF or capacity. It parses an exact `Content-Length`
header with at most nine decimal digits and rejects invalid values or bodies
shorter than the declared length. Absence of Content-Length remains valid for
connection-close framing. Redirects remain visible responses and are never
followed implicitly.

Browser and Node hosts do not expose the low socket/TLS ABI. They may link the
high-level `http_get` component import only through an explicit synchronous
fetch, worker or SharedArrayBuffer bridge. The bridge receives exact host,
port, path, output cap and `redirect: manual`; without injection the import is
absent and Wasm linking fails closed.

## Maturity boundary

Header-name matching for Content-Length is currently exact-case rather than
RFC case-insensitive. Transfer-Encoding chunked decoding, duplicate framing
header rejection, informational responses, external browser bridge E2E and
general browser component linking remain pending.
"}]
